WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:01.770
- [Mark] All right, Frankie.

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:02.603
Frankie, where'd you grow up?

00:00:02.603 --> 00:00:04.120
Where are you from, originally?

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:05.020
- Ohio.

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:05.853
- [Interviewer] Ohio?

00:00:05.853 --> 00:00:06.686
What city?

00:00:06.686 --> 00:00:08.070
- [Frankie] Cleveland.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.450
- [Mark] Cleveland?

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.723
And how long have you been in LA?

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.090
or California?

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:16.947
- California, 20 years.

00:00:16.947 --> 00:00:18.100
- [Mark] 20 years.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:21.500
- LA, about eight months.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.640
- [Mark] Were are you married?

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.473
- No.

00:00:23.473 --> 00:00:24.395
- Never married.
- No.

00:00:24.395 --> 00:00:25.470
- Do you have kids?
- No kids.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.140
- [Mark] No kids.

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.583
And what do you do for a living?

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.146
- I manage restaurants
and I did construction.

00:00:34.146 --> 00:00:35.330
- [Mark] Okay.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:36.540
You like to come down here to skid row

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.590
and pick up some of the ladies sometimes?

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.500
- Yeah, I do.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.200
Come down from Santa Monica

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:49.230
and that's pretty much
a place to come down.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:51.110
It's inexpensive

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.420
and if I have one drink

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:55.240
and maybe pick up some drugs,

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.870
mainly for ladies I don't
really do drugs anymore

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.920
but I have in the past.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.080
- [Mark] And you like to drink?

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.653
- Yes, I'm an alcoholic.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:05.830
- Tell me about your childhood.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:07.080
You had a good childhood?

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:10.630
- Nope.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.826
- [Mark] What kind of stuff went on?

00:01:12.826 --> 00:01:14.880
(sniffs loudly)

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.990
- Well, the only good thing
I can say about my childhood

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.850
is I wasn't ever abused

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:25.883
but my mom died when I was six.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.080
She was 36 years old

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:34.826
and my dad died at 46

00:01:36.803 --> 00:01:37.773
and I was 12.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:43.670
So I pretty much raised myself

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:47.290
and then I lived with a sister who was 21.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.460
She tried to raise me.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:51.470
I went to college for a couple of years.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:53.750
I held down some good jobs

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:57.103
but as far as childhood,
yeah, it wasn't good.

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.370
No abuse, no beatings.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.040
I've seen much worse
or something like that.

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.993
I just had parents who died too early.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:08.170
- [Mark] No, that's tragic.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:09.003
- Yep.

00:02:09.003 --> 00:02:09.963
- Twice.
- Yep.

00:02:11.818 --> 00:02:14.740
- [Mark] Do you feel like
that has impacted your life?

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:15.770
- Oh yeah.

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:16.920
- [Mark] To this day?

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.400
- Yep.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:19.993
- [Mark] In what ways do you think?

00:02:24.268 --> 00:02:25.101
(clears throat)

00:02:25.101 --> 00:02:27.743
- I had seven older brothers and sisters.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.143
Three sisters are dead.

00:02:38.419 --> 00:02:40.169
- [Mark] Here you go.

00:02:42.848 --> 00:02:43.848
- Thank you.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:49.803
Two brothers died.

00:02:51.509 --> 00:02:54.293
(sniffles) Everybody before they were 50.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.650
So I just thought

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.533
I was destined to die.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.580
So I lived my life kind of recklessly.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.193
Actually, I've had good jobs,

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:16.580
nice places to live,

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:17.723
good cars.

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.200
Then sometimes the wheels fall off

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.593
then I resort to my bad self.

00:03:25.126 --> 00:03:26.644
- [Mark] Which is usually drinking?

00:03:26.644 --> 00:03:28.727
- Yeah, drinking mainly.

00:03:29.587 --> 00:03:31.730
- [Mark] Thank you for sharing that.

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.340
- Yeah.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:35.120
- [Mark] That's terrible.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.240
- Yeah, I have done a
lot of drugs in the past

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:40.070
but not in the last couple of years.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.740
- [Mark] Did you go to college?

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:42.633
- Yes, I did.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:48.450
I graduated from high
school in Massachusetts

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:52.050
and I got accepted to Harvard

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:53.850
and I actually went through Harvard.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.721
Unfortunately it was in
the back of a police car.

00:03:57.721 --> 00:03:59.430
(both laugh)

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:03.360
But then after I got out, then
I actually went to college

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:06.030
in UMass Amherst

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.710
and I was doing really well

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.610
studying broadcast communication.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:14.040
I was a radio DJ.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.330
We had our own station out there.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.980
It only broadcasted to like
half the campus (sniffs).

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.168
I'm trying to think of what
my DJ name was, but anyway,

00:04:26.168 --> 00:04:27.910
(sniffs) that escapes me.

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:31.380
But then I came out here
for a two month vacation,

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:34.220
visited my brother up in Santa Cruz,

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:36.030
fell in love with a girl

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:42.130
and unfortunately didn't
go back finish college.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.930
And this was in the eighties,

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.990
and back then you didn't think
you really needed college.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:50.670
If I have my advice for anybody,

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.050
get an education,

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:53.883
get a trade, stay in school.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:57.233
You won't end up a fool.

00:04:57.233 --> 00:04:59.210
(Mark laughs)

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:00.160
- [Mark] So you come down here

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:01.860
to visit the ladies sometimes, right?

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.270
- Yeah.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:04.320
- [Mark] And how's that go for you?

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.670
You know, I've heard all kinds of stories.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.360
I've heard stories of
girls robbing the guys.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.820
I've heard stories of guys
getting rough with the girls

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:10.780
or robbing them,

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:11.730
all kinds of stuff.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:18.810
- Well, what I usually look for is,

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:21.690
I can usually tell in her face

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:23.690
or interactions

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.090
and I'm pretty careful.

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:29.620
And I've actually met a couple girls

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:32.520
in a bar or in a park

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:36.030
and they kind of turned
me on to someplace safe.

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:37.790
So when I come down here there's only

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:41.470
maybe two or three girls that I look for.

00:05:41.470 --> 00:05:43.440
If I don't see 'em then I leave.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.360
- [Mark] These are your regulars.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:45.783
- Yep.

00:05:45.783 --> 00:05:46.671
- [Mark] And you trust them?

00:05:46.671 --> 00:05:48.088
- Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.860
And usually, like I said, if I get drugs

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.933
I give them to them because
I don't do drugs anymore, so.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:59.980
But you know, it's all a barter system.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:02.520
Everything is for sale down here.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:03.710
- [Mark] Right.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:05.870
So you guys would go to
the car, you go to a hotel,

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:07.200
where do you guys go?

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.330
- Well, I'm from Santa Monica.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:11.300
I used to drive down here.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:14.160
Unfortunately I had my car repossessed.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:16.773
I still do have a place in Santa Monica.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.040
And I, when I come down here,

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.490
I take the train and the bus down here

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.440
and I usually come down
here like once a week

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.133
and I see some people down here.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.590
And it's a little bit easier
to access services down here.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:33.890
- [Mark] Yeah, easy to get around.

00:06:33.890 --> 00:06:34.723
- Yep.

00:06:35.638 --> 00:06:36.610
- [Mark] Do you ever feel

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.630
like you would prefer a committed
relationship, a marriage,

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.400
something like that?

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:42.630
- Too old for that.

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:43.930
- [Mark] Too old for that?

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:45.080
- Yep.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:46.690
- [Mark] And you like
the freedom and variety

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:47.930
that this provides?

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:49.030
- Yep.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:53.890
Well, because I used to
have, you know it all,

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:55.700
a nice place, a nice job

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:00.640
but it was called responsibility.

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:03.480
And you know, now I don't have anything.

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:06.250
I don't have any responsibility.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:07.250
Not saying that's good.

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:09.023
I don't like living on the street,

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:14.090
but at the same time (sniffs)

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:16.310
I don't have the problem with

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.840
an employer,

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.617
showing up for a job (sniffs),

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:23.940
a girlfriend

00:07:25.230 --> 00:07:28.093
and I can do what I like
to do, which is drink.

00:07:29.640 --> 00:07:30.473
- [Mark] And you usually get drunk

00:07:30.473 --> 00:07:32.180
before you pick up the girls.

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:33.610
- Always, yeah.
- Always (laughs)

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:34.720
- Yeah (sniffs).

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:38.316
And I always gotta check to
make sure they're not a guy, so.

00:07:38.316 --> 00:07:39.570
- [Mark] Oh, has that happened before?

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:40.743
- Oh yeah, yeah.

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:44.370
You can usually tell by the Adam's Apple

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:46.163
but then sometimes it's, you know,

00:07:47.207 --> 00:07:49.340
there were some that
looked pretty much like

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:52.233
a woman (sniffs) so.

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:57.390
- [Mark] What's the most
and least you've paid

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.390
for a girl out here?

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:02.440
- Oh, I've paid like a
six pack of beer (sniffs)

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:04.463
and probably the most,

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.587
when I had money, $200,
but that was an error.

00:08:08.587 --> 00:08:09.420
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.350
- I was in Vegas.

00:08:10.350 --> 00:08:11.430
- [Mark] Different neighborhood.

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:13.879
- Yeah, yeah, different place,

00:08:13.879 --> 00:08:14.920
different lifestyle

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:16.500
- [Mark] This is the least
expensive you'll find?

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:18.600
- Oh yeah, that's why I come down here.

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:20.330
Oh, I can go down to Santa Monica

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:22.455
but they're gonna be 50 bucks down there.

00:08:22.455 --> 00:08:24.330
(sniffs) I can come down here,

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:25.810
there's a couple I know 10 bucks

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.520
or I'd bring down some food

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:30.973
and a, you know, a bottle of wine,

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:34.410
you know, they were mine
for a couple of hours.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:40.200
Sometimes I can get some
vouchers for a hotel

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.010
and that's even better.

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:42.843
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:48.160
- So not too proud of what I do but

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:52.330
you know, we have our baser instincts and

00:08:56.380 --> 00:08:58.130
sometimes you gotta follow 'em.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:08:59.080
- [Mark] Yeah, there's many different ways

00:08:59.080 --> 00:09:00.660
of looking at prostitution.

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.910
There are those that say,

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:05.220
no one's getting hurt.

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:06.780
It's okay.

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:08.123
Both parties agreed to it.

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:12.400
You'll see people taking
opposing sides on that.

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:14.910
- Well--
- It's a very complex topic.

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:17.880
- Yeah, I don't really want
to get into it but I think

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:24.570
if the woman's forced into it,

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:25.420
then it's wrong,

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:29.400
if she does it on her own...
- Yeah, that's (mumbles)

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:34.400
- And I don't think it's the
old days where you see guys,

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:38.260
the pimps, slapping around
the girls and dragging them in

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:40.647
and around and stuff like that (sniffs).

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:46.710
But unfortunately a lot
of them have drug problems

00:09:50.486 --> 00:09:54.290
and

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.130
I don't really ask them
about their history but

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:02.610
it probably involves a
lot of abuse (sniffs)

00:10:02.610 --> 00:10:03.443
and

00:10:08.090 --> 00:10:09.500
they just need to get by,

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:12.100
they just need to do what
they need to do to get by.

00:10:15.850 --> 00:10:17.350
- [Mark] Looking back at your life

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:21.083
and the tragedies that
you had to go through.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:23.540
You've had jobs.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:26.720
You've survived nicely.

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:29.000
What do you attribute that to?

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:30.753
What's your view on surviving?

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:35.810
- Well I've always liked to work

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:37.293
and I'd like to keep busy.

00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:39.630
- [Mark] And that keeps you on track?

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:40.463
- Yep.

00:10:40.463 --> 00:10:41.810
- [Mark] Despite the alcohol and?

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:43.470
- Yeah.

00:10:43.470 --> 00:10:46.040
And if I got money and
nothing to do (sniffs),

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.510
then I go drink.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:49.400
But if I got a job,

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.470
I'll go work all day and
then I'll get off of work

00:10:51.470 --> 00:10:54.423
and drink and then go
to work the next day.

00:10:55.274 --> 00:10:56.125
(sniffs loudly)

00:10:56.125 --> 00:10:58.420
It did always help that
I've always worked in

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.890
bars and restaurants.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:06.890
So it was acceptable for
me to be around alcohol.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.060
And as a bartender

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.793
you would actually have
to taste the drinks.

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:12.903
So...

00:11:15.075 --> 00:11:16.980
- [Mark] Have you ever had a girlfriend?

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:17.813
- Many.

00:11:17.813 --> 00:11:18.646
- [Man] Long term.
- Yep.

00:11:18.646 --> 00:11:20.570
- [Mark] A long-term girlfriend?

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.360
And those relationships were
successful, they were good?

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:24.733
- Yep.

00:11:24.733 --> 00:11:26.360
(sniffs loudly)

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:28.810
You know, maybe it was my upbringing

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:33.673
but I never really wanted to have kids.

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:37.250
And I've actually had three

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:39.540
eight-year relationships with women

00:11:40.660 --> 00:11:42.110
and they were great,

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:43.290
they were beautiful women,

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:44.843
I was lucky to be with them.

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:49.740
But kind of after like
the sixth, seventh year

00:11:49.740 --> 00:11:51.790
they started saying, well,
when are we gonna get married,

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:53.750
when are we gonna get married?

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:55.590
And usually after like eight years,

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:56.510
I don't know what it is,

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:59.960
the 8 year itch or whatever,
you know, it was just,

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:03.310
I didn't wanna hold 'em back.

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:05.460
They wanted to have
kids, I didn't want to.

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:07.833
So,

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:10.600
they were some beautiful women.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:14.520
- [Mark] All right, Frankie.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.140
Well, thank you so much
for talking with me.

00:12:16.140 --> 00:12:17.090
- Okay.

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.410
- [Mark] Good luck with
the rest of your life.

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:19.560
- Thank you.
- Thanks.

